{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpretation recorded for the fixed VerifyLeader experiment. Successor receipt 68e243c33c644a32bc7ec9b29f076623 is complete: comparison 0 (treatment anomaly prediction) holds over the three independent attempts at indices 2, 6, 9, where the partitioned leader — quorum 2 over voters {leader, far1, far2} with one demoted non-voter reachable — answered VerifyLeader with nil while still Leader; both controls hold (index 12, same reachable node still a voter, quorum 3; index 15, non-voter also cut off), each returning 'leadership lost while committing log' at ~1.98s. The earlier receipt shows the same pattern (2, 5, 8 vs 11, 14) and is cited with joint_history. Scoped defect claim asserted: VerifyLeader's confirmation is satisfied by an acknowledgement from a peer the target itself defines as not considered for elections or commitment, so a client gating reads on it can be told a leader that has lost every voter but itself is still leader until its own lease expires. Counterevidence and limits kept explicitly (no competing leader at the instant of confirmation; index 3 shows the majority committed a write absent from the partitioned leader's FSM, but only after that leader had become Follower), and the open gap about whether the false confirmation can outlive the lease window is left unanswered for a follow-up with per-node timing.\"}"}}
